  {
   "slug": "autumn-tour-twelve-cities",
   "title": "Autumn Tour: Twelve Cities, One Van",
   "date": "2026-09-29T12:00:00",
   "excerpt": "The full route, what we are bringing, and why the van has a name.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We are taking Midnight Signal on the road this autumn: twelve cities in five weeks, in the same van that took us around the clubs three years ago. She is called Marlene, she has a cassette player, and she has never let us down.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The new show has a lighting rig we built ourselves, a longer set and, for the first time, a few songs from the first record played the way we always wanted to play them.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Good to know</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Doors open at 19:30, support at 20:15, we play at 21:15.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Every show is all ages unless the venue says otherwise.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Merch takes cards; we bring our own small stock of vinyl.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The van smells of coffee, cables and optimism.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Tour diary, day one</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Tickets are on the tour page. A few dates are close to selling out, so do not wait too long.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "tour"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "tour-diary"
   ],
   "featured_media": "tour-van",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": "Pia",
     "email": "pia@example.com",
     "content": "Long live Marlene the van.",
     "date": "2026-09-30T03:00:00"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "slug": "inside-the-studio-midnight-signal",
   "title": "Inside the Studio: Building Midnight Signal",
   "date": "2026-08-14T18:30:00",
   "excerpt": "Two old synthesizers, one borrowed drum kit and a mixing desk with a mind of its own.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>People keep asking how we got the sound of this record, so here is the honest answer: mostly by accident, and partly by refusing to throw anything away.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The core of the album is two old analogue synthesizers we have owned since we were teenagers. One of them only stays in tune when it is cold, which is why so many songs were recorded in winter with the heating off.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:columns --><div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:studio-console}}\" alt=\"A mixing console with faders and glowing level meters\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">The desk</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:mic-spotlight}}\" alt=\"A vintage microphone alone in a spotlight\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">One mic for every vocal</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What we learned</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Record the rehearsal. The rehearsal is usually better.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Two good microphones beat ten average ones.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>If a song needs a fourth chorus, it needs a better second verse.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We mixed the record ourselves over six long weeks. The meters spent a lot of time in the red, and we would not change a thing.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "studio"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "midnight-signal",
    "gear"
   ],
   "featured_media": "studio-console",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": []
  },
  {
   "slug": "festival-season-recap",
   "title": "Festival Season, in Twelve Pictures",
   "date": "2026-07-30T10:15:00",
   "excerpt": "Seven festivals, three countries, one very muddy Sunday.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>What a summer. We played seven festivals, from a tiny tent in a forest to the second stage of a field big enough to have its own weather system. Thank you to everyone who stood in the rain to watch us.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The highlight was the Sunday evening slot at the coastal festival, when the sun came out exactly as we started Afterglow. You cannot plan that. We tried.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:gallery {\"columns\":3,\"linkTo\":\"none\",\"align\":\"wide\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-3 is-cropped alignwide\"><!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:festival-field}}\" alt=\"A festival crowd with raised arms under white searchlights at sunset\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:crowd-lights}}\" alt=\"A crowd facing a stage lit with coloured beams\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:band-silhouette}}\" alt=\"Four band members in silhouette against a magenta glow\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --></figure><!-- /wp:gallery --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Next year we would like to play somewhere with less mud. We say that every year.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "tour"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "tour-diary",
    "live"
   ],
   "featured_media": "festival-field",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": []
