  {
   "slug": "b-sides-on-vinyl",
   "title": "The B-Sides Are Coming to Vinyl",
   "date": "2026-06-18T15:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Eight songs that never fit anywhere, pressed on violet vinyl in an edition of five hundred.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Every band has a folder of songs that did not fit. Ours finally gets a home: eight B-sides and demos from the last five years, collected on a single record.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Some of them are rough, one of them was recorded on a phone in a hotel corridor, and two of them are among our favourite things we have ever made.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\",\"align\":\"wide\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image alignwide size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:b-sides-vinyl}}\" alt=\"A violet record sleeve marked B-Sides beside a black vinyl record\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Five hundred copies, violet vinyl</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Pre-orders open on the first of next month, and every copy comes with a hand-numbered insert.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "news"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "release",
    "vinyl"
   ],
   "featured_media": "b-sides-vinyl",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": []
  },
  {
   "slug": "new-video-filmed-in-one-take",
   "title": "A New Video, Filmed in One Take",
   "date": "2026-05-22T19:45:00",
   "excerpt": "Three minutes and forty seconds, one camera, no cuts and a lot of rehearsal.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The video for Static Hearts was filmed in a single continuous shot, in an empty car park, at four in the morning. It took eleven attempts. The seventh was nearly perfect until a fox walked through.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Our friend who directed it built the neon grid on the ground from LED strips and tape. We danced, badly but bravely, and the camera never stopped moving.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:pullquote --><figure class=\"wp-block-pullquote\"><blockquote><p>We did eleven takes. The fox was in the best one, so we kept it.</p></blockquote></figure><!-- /wp:pullquote --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Watch it loud, and look out for the fox at 2:41.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "news"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "video",
    "midnight-signal"
   ],
   "featured_media": "neon-grid",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": []
  },
  {
   "slug": "how-we-mix-the-live-show",
   "title": "How We Mix the Live Show",
   "date": "2026-04-09T11:30:00",
   "excerpt": "Our front-of-house engineer explains why the show sounds bigger than four people should.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We asked our sound engineer to explain the live mix. Her first answer was that she turns the bass up until the venue manager comes over. Her second answer was more useful.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Every show starts from the same saved desk file, adjusted for the room during soundcheck. The synths go through their own small sub-mix so they can be pushed together without drowning the vocals.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} --><ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Vocals first: if the words are lost, nothing else matters.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Leave space between the kick drum and the bass synth.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Use the room: small clubs need less, not more.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ol><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>And yes, earplugs. Please wear earplugs. We want to see you at the next tour too.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "studio"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "gear",
    "live"
   ],
   "featured_media": "waveform",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": []
  }
 ],
